commit b0163e0127374a50ca753f6cd38a998f3374f34d
Author: admin <admin@MacBook-Pro-de-admin.local>
Date:   Mon Aug 24 13:09:32 2026 -0400

    feat: RammRegistry — fix a shared contract without redeploying every market
    
    The real problem behind two full 49+8-market redeploys already done this
    project: IMPXMarket stored RAMMToken, RedemptionNFT, VestingVault, and
    PromoStaking as immutable addresses set at construction. Fixing any one
    of those four meant deploying a new version AND redeploying every market
    that referenced the old address — free but annoying on testnet, and a
    genuine dead end on mainnet, where it would mean stranding real user
    funds on markets that can never be pointed at the fix.
    
    RammRegistry is the standard answer (same shape as Aave's
    PoolAddressesProvider / Compound's Comptroller registry pattern): one
    small contract holding mutable pointers to the four shared singletons,
    with onlyOwner setters. IMPXMarket now stores only the registry's own
    address as immutable, and resolves the four dependencies fresh on every
    call via _rammToken()/_redemptionNFT()/_vestingVault()/_promoStaking()
    internal helpers. Rolling out a fix to any of the four is now one
    setX() call on the registry — every market, old and new, picks it up
    on its next call, no redeploy. Also simplifies IMPXMarket's constructor
    from 14 params down to 11.
    
    The existing authorizedMarkets allow-list pattern on VestingVault/
    RedemptionNFT/RAMMToken is unchanged and still necessary — the registry
    solves "how does a market find the current vault," authorizedMarkets
    solves "which markets can call the vault." Complementary, not redundant.
    
    Proven with a new test, not just asserted: deploys a second VestingVault
    mid-test, points the *already-deployed* market at it via
    registry.setVestingVault(), and confirms a referral credit lands in the
    new vault with zero changes to the market contract.
    (test_Registry_SwapVestingVault_NoMarketRedeployNeeded)
    
    Updated all three deployment paths that actually construct IMPXMarket —
    Deploy.s.sol (reference script), agents/src/scripts/deployDemoProducts.ts
    and migrateCampaignContracts.ts (the real bulk-deployment paths), and
    VALET's live createCampaign() flow — to deploy/wire a registry instead
    of passing the four addresses directly. All read from REGISTRY_ADDRESS.
    
    62/62 contract tests passing (58 existing + 4 new registry tests).
    Not yet redeployed to Base Sepolia or migrated onto the live 49+8
    markets — that's a real operational step (touches every product this
    app has been tested against all session), holding for explicit go-ahead
    before running it.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

